WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-DE

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.440
Hello.  Welcome back to Lam Rim.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.580
Today's session is a review of the entire course.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.520
That's good for me.  I would like to do a repeat performance for myself as well.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.680
In this format, where we produce individual episodes,

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.400
one after the other, at different times,

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.100
the flow of the entire instruction can be lost.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.880
Therefore, I think it's good if we start all over again

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.560
and then

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.640
repeat the entire previous Lam Rim instruction in one go.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:43.000
I use IDIMs for this, the idea pictures

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.360
we use to teach the ACI teachers.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.980
ACI teachers

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:52.800
are expected to be able to see one of the images

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.300
and identify the underlying concept.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.580
Tim, how many IDIMs do we have?  1,000 or so?  How many

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.800
?

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:09.300
500, something like that. So it's very easy to give an exam,

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.160
to test someone; we simply use the images.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.340
We'll just show you these pictures.  So,

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.800
in this repetition, I challenge you:

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.240
when we show a picture,

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.000
I give you one second and you see if you

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.533
can remember what the picture was about?

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.440
This is a good review of

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.800
this entire course.  Okay, let's begin.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.000
First picture, Mr. Sejii.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.240
This image is meant to remind you

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:47.420
that we are in the middle of the practices

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.360
for people with medium motivation,

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.180
and what they want is to reach Nirvana.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:59.160
They want to break free from the cycle of life, from all the suffering, for themselves alone.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.140
For this purpose, Buddha taught the three practices

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.120
that will help you reach your personal Nirvana.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:12.420
The third training is: understanding emptiness, understanding the pen.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.880
The second training is meditation.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:21.200
These two can only be truly deep in a quiet place,

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:27.300
at certain times of day, when you are really focused on your meditation mat.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.740
These two need to be taken really deep

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.420
at specific times of day.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:39.360
But the third one, the basis for the other two, being kind to others,

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.480
you can also call it morality,

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.100
you can call it an ethical way of life,

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.800
but in the end, it is being kind to others:

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.840
that is the basis

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.700
that is always available to us, all day long.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.900
This is one of the three extraordinary trainings of Buddhism,

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.820
and it is supposed to help us reach Nirvana.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.960
And it's available to us all day.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.480
In this picture

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.360
you can see Sejii helping Geshe Michael get to grips with his computer.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:15.160
Which is one of the kindest things young people can do for older people.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:21.320
Next picture.  See if you can remember what the picture means.  Do

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.040
you have any guesses?

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:34.080
This woman is doing her taxes.
Why is she doing this work in the Lam Rim system?

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.540
It makes her...

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:41.620
a Dharma master.  When I say Dharma Master or Tantra Master,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.500
I can already see the image in your head:

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.460
a high lama, on a large throne with a large yellow hat.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:55.240
Perhaps he or she is holding a bell and a small drum and reciting mantras.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.760
And you think: "Oh, that's a Dharma Master. That's a real Dharma Master."

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.420
Or you could imagine the old image of Nagarjuna,

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:07.080
so mystical.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:11.220
But in Lam Rim we learned

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.220
that this woman, who

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.900
has children and is married,

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:22.260
is a Dharma Master.  She is a true Dharma master.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:27.620
Pabongka Rinpoche says: "Do not believe that a Dharma Master has to sit on a throne

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:31.120
and recite Tantra rituals."  What does

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.960
this woman do?

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.760
She pays her taxes.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:43.100
Being honest about taxes is really difficult in my country.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:46.700
It can take you weeks to do your taxes properly, to

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.880


00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.200
make them completely honest, to

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.020
pay every single penny you are owed.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.400
That's what makes her...

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:00.560
she has the first of the extraordinary trainings of a good person,

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:02.720
being kind to others.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.280
That makes her a true Dharma master.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:09.760
So forget those pictures of llamas with big hats

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.500
ringing bells.  That's easy.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:13.260
Anyone can do it.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.720
Being kind to others is difficult.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.280
And upholding your morals, your ethics,

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.060
is also difficult.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:24.700
The next image:

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:30.780
I'll give you a moment.   Do
you remember what this is about?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.240
The quote in the Lam Rim is:
TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.560
A person who truly keeps his vows,

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.880
truly keeps his Buddhist guidelines, especially the 10 guidelines,

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.620
he shines, he truly shines.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:58.656
A person who makes the healthy, modest, and reserved effort to keep their promises, to do

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.640
the 10 good karmas, and to be kind

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.000
to others,

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.760
has a kind of peaceful look on their face;

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.040
they radiate joy.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.380
When someone like that comes into the room, you know it.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:17.360
Everyone feels better, just like with Tim and Seijii.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.860
This is the light of the world.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.440
Buddha says these people are the light of the world.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.380
There is a Christian saying: Do

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:32.400
n't hide your light under a bushel, let the world see your happy face.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:39.960
And that is a true, guiding light for the entire world.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.740
The next picture, IDIM 4,

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:58.100
is a mountain cliff where I was with my partner Veronika on her birthday during this Lam Rim.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:06.940
The conversation was about the sunset,
in Tibetan NUB PA.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:10.600
This also means "west", because the sun sets in the west.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.500
NUB PA means

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.340
the sun is setting, and that is a very sad verb.

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:21.040
That is a very sad thought in Dharma.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:27.520
The most famous passage is at the end of the Abhidharmakosha, "Treasury of Higher Wisdom".

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:32.060
"Treasury of Higher Knowledge" by Master Vasubhandu.  He says in it:

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:39.060
"The sun of Dharma, the light of Dharma, will set in the world."

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:43.440
We will lose the light of Dharma in this world.  This world will fall into darkness.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.520
After a certain period of time,

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.560
the teachings of the Buddha will disappear from this world.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:56.020
First they will disappear from people's minds, but they will still exist in libraries.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:59.840
These books will still be in the libraries.  Probably in libraries that John Brady hasn't found yet.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:04.240
And later they will have disappeared from the libraries as well.  And then they will be gone.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:12.200
I chose this image because Pabongka Rinpoche emphasized something special here.  He says:

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:19.520
"If you cannot keep your promises, if you cannot behave kindly towards others,

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.820
then we can say that the Dharma has left this world."

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:26.520
The light of Dharma has left this world within you.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.780
The sun has set in your own breast,

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:34.460
which would be a very sad thing if we do not keep our promises.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:37.120
Next picture.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:48.520
This retreat is called: "Love in the Time of the Virus".

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:55.440
The point is: In difficult times in the world,

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.600
if you keep your promises,

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:00.860
if you are kind to others,

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.320
in times when things are scary and eerie, when the virus is spreading,

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.580
nobody knows where, nobody knows how,

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:09.440
nobody knows how many people will die.  Doing

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:16.820
something kind for others during these difficult times

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.160
is all the more powerful.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:22.800
He mentions, if you remember, a 5-star Buddha paradise,

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.960
the perfect place:

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:30.040
It's easy to be a good person there,
everyone is a good person there.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:33.240
That's not a great achievement.  It's not a big deal

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.380
and the seed isn't that powerful:

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.580
being friendly in a group of friendly people.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:43.320
Being kind when people attack you, when they are afraid,

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:47.880
when others are not kind to each other, if you are that person

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:54.060
who stands up and shares things with others in difficult times,

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.920
then you are an extremely pure person.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:01.080
That's great karma.  That's incredible karma, much more powerful.

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:04.040
I think the virus is a very good time,

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:09.120
a very good opportunity for all of us to show

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:14.380
whether we are truly Buddhists,
whether we truly practice the Bodhisattva path.  Can

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:18.560
we help others, even when everything is extremely difficult?

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.500
Next picture.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:31.260
This is difficult to remember; I have trouble with it myself.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:36.280
I'll give you a second to figure out what this picture represents.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:44.220
Pabongka Rinpoche quoted from several works,

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:48.800
which, as different as they are, all have the same typical ending:

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:57.320
He quotes a famous ending: BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA ... CIG, which means:

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:02.720
May the teachings of the Victorious One,

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.780
Lobsang Drakpa, Je Tsongkapa,

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:08.080
spread throughout this world.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:12.720
You think: We have to put this on the internet!

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:16.420
We need to translate this Lam Rim into many languages.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:22.080
We must try to bring these good words to as many people as possible.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:31.020
This is the end of the prayer, and now, after the end of this Lam Rim class or video, we should

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:35.340
share the Dharma with others.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:38.280
We are meant to spread the Dharma throughout the world.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:43.880
In this part of the Lam Rim, Pabongka Rinpoche says:

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:50.660
"The place where you should spread the Dharma is here, in your own heart."  Do

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:55.700
n't think that "spreading Dharma" means translating the videos

00:11:55.900 --> 00:12:00.800
into even more languages ​​or anything like that.
Yes, it is important to spread the Dharma in this way.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:05.460
But he says: If you spread it in your own heart,

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:10.080
then of course it will also spread outside of you, because the world comes from your heart,

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:12.360
or more precisely: from your heart chakra.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:17.180
Next picture, number 7.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:23.420
Try to remember what this picture was about.  I'll give you a few seconds.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:31.800
This is one of my favorite topics:

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:42.000
the personal relationship with another person, as these two people have it.  In

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:47.860
my opinion, and in Tantra, it is one of the most beautiful things that can happen to you.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:51.860
It's one of the greatest things you can experience.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:57.520
Anyone can tell you why the whole world is looking for a partner:

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:00.280
because it makes people happy.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:03.520
It is one of the greatest joys when things go well.

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:07.520
It is one of the greatest joys you can experience,

00:13:08.399 --> 00:13:12.799
but you and I also know:
when things don't go well,

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.360
it is one of the greatest sufferings in life.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.160
Why is this relevant to this course right now?

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:29.120
If your ethics are good,

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:31.580
it is the greatest happiness in your life.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:36.680
And if you break your ethics, the same thing will make you unhappy.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:40.320
If you have a good woman or a good man as a partner,

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.620
then the same person who makes you totally happy can

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.220
also make you totally unhappy.

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:52.560
So in this case, Vinaya, your personal practice of kindness,

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:56.240
of good behavior, is compared to a partner

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:59.980
who brings out in you either the best you can be in this life

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.320
or the worst - the same person.

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:08.180
Next IDIM, number 8.

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:14.180
That was a complicated picture.  Do you remember?

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:17.900
I take a sip of my green smoothie.

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:20.640
Thank you, Vimala.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:33.560
This is about breaking your promises.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.240
Pulling up weeds represents breaking your promises.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:45.260
Why does the destruction of this plant symbolize the breaking of your promises?

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:51.560
If you are a gardener, you know that you must remove the weeds

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:54.780
before their seeds ripen.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:59.380
If you wait until the seeds are about to fall off

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.920
and only then remove the plant,

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:04.740
you will spread thousands of seeds.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:11.060
And a month, a year later, you will see a thousand times more weeds sprouting.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.440
So you need to pull out these weeds early.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:19.140
This refers to a very radical statement

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.360
made by the Buddha:

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:27.900
DGE SLONG DAG SROG DANG BRAL ZHING SHI BA NI BLA'I

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.240
Better to die

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.479
than to break your promises.  How come?

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.680
If you break your promises,

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.980
you will sow seeds

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.660
that will multiply for many lifetimes.

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:49.740
If you die now, you have ruined a mind-body connection.

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:54.060
If you die now, you will ruin a very useful temple,

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:57.360
a body temple, and a spirit temple.
You will lose ONE such connection.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.560
But if you break your promises,

00:16:01.279 --> 00:16:04.440
you lose many mind-body connections.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.458
You're ruining body and mind for many lifetimes.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:11.440
You are planting seeds

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.280
that will ruin many lives.

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:20.420
Buddha said: It is better to die than to break your promises.

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:27.460
And he didn't mean that metaphorically.
He meant it quite literally

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:31.280
when he said: Better to die than to break your promises!  There's

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:35.360
this joke in Lam Rim.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:44.320
We take a vow never to give up Bodhichitta, not even if it costs us our lives.  There's

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:52.480
this famous saying:
Our whole lives we expect to be

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.720
put in prison

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.880
by some evil people.

00:16:57.199 --> 00:17:02.479
They threaten you with a knife and say: "Abandon your Bodhisattva vows, or you will die now!"

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.799
And we then reply:

00:17:04.799 --> 00:17:06.480
"I choose death!"

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:09.199
And they are killing us.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.280
I think we've all been waiting for a situation like this since we took that vow.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:18.300
We're waiting for these guys to show up with knives and threaten us.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:22.960
But actually, WE are the guys with the knives.  We threaten our Bodhisattva vows every day.

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:31.840
Every day we have to make the decision whether or not to carefully keep our promises.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.860
It's difficult to find those types who will put you in prison and say,

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.440
"I will kill you if you don't renounce your Bodhisattva vows."

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.720
Next picture.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:54.540
See if you can remember.  I'll give you a moment, try to remember.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:05.840
That was a hint at...

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.039
In our "Mixed Nuts" translator team,

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:12.559
we translated an old Vinaya test:

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.440
The monks' and nuns' vows.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:25.140
It was about the vow, the tradition we are not supposed to break:

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:29.820
When you become a monk or nun, you get your robe,

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.840
a small Buddhist statue,

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.960
and a sieve.

00:18:35.919 --> 00:18:39.279
In ancient India, you always had to have this sieve with you.

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:43.360
To drink water from a river,

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:49.439
you should first filter the water to ensure that you don't kill any small insects.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.680
We have mentioned a famous tradition from the Vinaya:

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:59.200
When some monks go to the water,

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:02.380
to the river, to fetch water,

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:07.340
they should choose the friendliest monk to test the water.  Do

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:15.040
n't choose the guy who doesn't care about insects.  Take the one who loves insects,

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:19.280
let him test the water, for he will be more attentive.  What is this about

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:22.000
?

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:26.440
We talked about "ecological vows,"

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:31.540
where monks and nuns are not even allowed to tear the leaves off a plant

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:37.560
because they are home to tiny creatures.

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:43.000
It means that you must respect even the smallest vows;

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:49.180
take them very seriously, because the results will increase exponentially.

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:53.600
Furthermore, it is important to maintain your ethics at a very subtle level,

00:19:55.039 --> 00:19:58.399
at a very refined level.  And please: Don't overdo it!

00:20:00.559 --> 00:20:02.549
If I were to write the Bodhisattva vows,

00:20:02.549 --> 00:20:04.719
I would include an extra Bodhisattva vow about

00:20:05.039 --> 00:20:07.199
not overdoing it with your Bodhisattva vows.

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.840
There's nothing more annoying

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:14.420
than a person informing you that they are keeping their vows

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:17.760
and therefore have to be an asshole today.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:23.199
Keep your vows in a loving way. Joyfully.  Don't overdo it.  Do

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:29.760
n't bother other people with your vows.  The vows are not meant to bother other people with them.

00:20:30.559 --> 00:20:35.279
Keep the small vows, keep them quietly, personally, don't make a demonstration out of them.

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:42.159
There is an expression in Islam: Don't let the right hand know what the left hand is doing.

00:20:43.039 --> 00:20:46.799
It means that you should not ostentatiously display your vows.  Keep them still and quiet.

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:49.840
And at a very high level.

00:20:50.559 --> 00:20:52.559
Next picture.  The point

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:04.780
here is that being kind to others

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:08.900
is like planting a tree.

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:12.020
Today I went to the PeachTree Cafe to

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:14.740
check something.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:19.039
Stanley, Allison and I planted a peach tree there

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:23.599
when we first did the PeachTree Cafe Morning Show.

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:28.319
I want to tell you that 3 peaches grew on it this week;

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:31.359
we now have peaches.

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:38.820
This means: Pay attention to your basic practice.

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:43.160
Pay attention to the root.  Plant kind karma

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:46.440
by keeping your vows, by being kind to others.

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:48.480
A tree will grow from it.

00:21:49.039 --> 00:21:51.039
And the peach tree that we

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:53.760
planted about 5 months ago is

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:56.559
already bearing lots of fruit.

00:21:57.200 --> 00:22:03.540
If you hadn't taken care of him when he was little, you wouldn't have anything now.

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:06.860
If you take care of the foundation of your Buddhist practice,

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.360
being kind to others,

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:12.800
then you will reap thousands of fruits.

00:22:12.860 --> 00:22:14.820
That's how it will be.  It will grow

00:22:14.820 --> 00:22:16.640
into a huge tree

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:22.080
that produces peaches every year.
You will have peaches for years to come.

00:22:22.640 --> 00:22:24.140
Hold and protect them.

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:28.160
This child in the picture has carefully protected the seedling.

00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:30.480
Protect your ethics.

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:33.120
Next picture.

00:22:34.880 --> 00:22:39.960
If I remember correctly, there are 4 conditions

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:43.760
that can lead to you breaking your obligations.

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:45.760
If you have taken the Bodhisattva vows,

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:49.039
or the Vinaya Pratimoksha vows,

00:22:49.679 --> 00:22:52.399
or even the Diamond Way, the Tantra vows—

00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:58.799
I believe there were four—Pabongka Rinpoche summarized them... perhaps there were more...

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:01.440
anyway, there are specific conditions

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:03.740
that will help you break your vows.

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:07.880
If you want to break your vows, there are a few specific ways to do it.

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:08.960
Here's the first one:

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:15.060
If you don't know your vows,

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:19.700
that's a good indication that you'll break them.  If you want to break them,

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:21.300
then simply don't study them!

00:23:21.640 --> 00:23:25.600
One of the things that bothers me, and there are many things that bother me about the Dharma,

00:23:26.660 --> 00:23:32.360
is teachers who give initiations, major initiations,

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:37.200
but they don't explain to the people taking the initiations

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:40.120
that they have just taken vows.

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:43.380
When you undergo an initiation, there are hundreds of vows that you take at the same time,

00:23:44.320 --> 00:23:46.960
and you will break them if you don't know them.

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:49.780
It is the teacher's responsibility to teach

00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:54.000
you the vows before you receive initiation.

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:59.520
If he or she does not offer you such instruction, then I would not accept any initiation from him or her.

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:05.760
The best way to break your vow, the first way, is not to know it.

00:24:06.160 --> 00:24:08.000
Read the recipe before you start cooking.

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:11.280
Veronica tells me that every time I cook.

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:14.640
Next picture.

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:21.980
A woman who says: "It's not a big deal."

00:24:22.140 --> 00:24:32.200
This vow, not to cut any leaves without prayer, come on,

00:24:32.940 --> 00:24:39.020
that's really extreme.  That's a bit too much, not that important.

00:24:39.020 --> 00:24:41.520
It's just about a few insects

00:24:41.680 --> 00:24:46.140
that might occasionally use this leaf as a roof.

00:24:46.140 --> 00:24:48.720
It's not a big deal.

00:24:49.080 --> 00:24:52.360
The second major way to break your vows

00:24:52.560 --> 00:24:54.010
is precisely this attitude:

00:24:54.010 --> 00:24:57.839
"Oh, the vow isn't that important, I'd rather keep the important ones."

00:24:58.799 --> 00:25:00.799
The next picture.

00:25:04.880 --> 00:25:11.020
When we have a Klesha attack, when something negative

00:25:11.360 --> 00:25:15.440
dominates our mind, it's an excellent opportunity to break our vows:

00:25:15.600 --> 00:25:19.180
becoming angry at someone

00:25:19.600 --> 00:25:24.920
or something, wanting to have it desperately, e.g., money,

00:25:25.200 --> 00:25:28.080
or being addicted to Netflix every night.

00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:34.680
...By the way, there's nothing wrong with watching Netflix, but what I'm talking about is

00:25:37.500 --> 00:25:41.840
hurting someone because you desperately want to go home to watch Netflix.  That's the problem here.

00:25:43.360 --> 00:25:45.447
This picture is called Gang Fighting.

00:25:45.447 --> 00:25:49.000
What's the story behind it?

00:25:50.800 --> 00:25:54.720
Always go after the biggest guy in the opposing gang first.

00:25:55.520 --> 00:25:57.520
Find out who the leader of the other side is, do

00:25:58.160 --> 00:26:02.660
n't argue, don't negotiate, don't shout at each other,

00:26:02.740 --> 00:26:05.520
go up to him and punch him.

00:26:06.080 --> 00:26:09.340
And then the entire opposing side will be defeated as well.

00:26:09.580 --> 00:26:13.660
Identify your biggest bad habit

00:26:13.760 --> 00:26:17.520
and take care of it first.  This is one way to keep your promises.

00:26:19.840 --> 00:26:21.840
The next picture.

00:26:23.880 --> 00:26:29.220
Incidentally, at my age—

00:26:29.220 --> 00:26:32.320
I won't tell you how old I am—

00:26:32.320 --> 00:26:35.760
this whole "young love" thing

00:26:35.760 --> 00:26:38.640
is so ridiculous from the perspective of my age.

00:26:40.960 --> 00:26:43.360
I can say that from experience, because I've experienced it myself.

00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:46.880
But this whole thing about:

00:26:46.880 --> 00:26:49.359
Oh, she's the most beautiful woman in the world.

00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:52.000
He is the most attractive man in the world.

00:26:53.040 --> 00:26:59.560
My older brother once said something funny:

00:26:59.560 --> 00:27:01.440
"You like the girl?"  I said "Yes".

00:27:02.080 --> 00:27:04.080
He asked: "Do you want to spend your life with her?"
I said "Yes".

00:27:04.640 --> 00:27:06.640
Then he said: "Look at her mother first.

00:27:07.679 --> 00:27:14.798
Look at what her mother looks like."  I said, "Your mother looks terrible. She is overweight, she looks tired and terrible."

00:27:15.440 --> 00:27:20.360
And he said, "What do you think she looked like before?"

00:27:20.720 --> 00:27:22.880
Think about it.

00:27:24.080 --> 00:27:28.160
If you are so fixated on a person's appearance,

00:27:28.880 --> 00:27:33.920
or something physical, something not really important about a person:

00:27:34.100 --> 00:27:38.860
that will change.  You will witness this person become ill and grow old.

00:27:38.860 --> 00:27:42.680
You will witness her having diarrhea and vomiting.

00:27:42.880 --> 00:27:46.720
If you're unlucky, you might see her intestines during an operation.  Do

00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:50.800
n't kid yourself, don't

00:27:51.760 --> 00:27:53.760
think it's worth hurting others to

00:27:54.320 --> 00:27:59.200
get the most beautiful woman or man ever.  It's not worth it.

00:28:00.480 --> 00:28:07.199
It won't stay that way.  It's wonderful to be in a relationship, but you should be in it for the right reasons.

00:28:07.840 --> 00:28:09.840
The next picture.

00:28:11.520 --> 00:28:13.759
If you have a problem with anger,

00:28:14.640 --> 00:28:16.640
or you get easily upset,

00:28:16.960 --> 00:28:19.600
then develop this fantasy of giving this person

00:28:20.320 --> 00:28:23.100
something they would like to have.

00:28:23.100 --> 00:28:26.080
That's called maître, jampa

00:28:26.080 --> 00:28:26.794
love.

00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:32.020
Develop this imagination, remember how wonderful it is to give someone something

00:28:32.560 --> 00:28:34.831
they like or want.

00:28:34.840 --> 00:28:36.880
Develop this attitude.

00:28:37.280 --> 00:28:40.720
If you are not well-disposed towards another person,

00:28:41.520 --> 00:28:44.419
then fantasize a little, meditate on

00:28:45.520 --> 00:28:49.039
how you can give that person something they truly desire.

00:28:49.679 --> 00:28:51.679
The next picture.

00:28:52.720 --> 00:28:58.559
I'll give you a moment, I bet you can't remember!

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.000
Tim cheats and flips ahead.

00:29:06.720 --> 00:29:08.720
What was this about?  For

00:29:09.600 --> 00:29:12.480
pride.

00:29:13.279 --> 00:29:16.398
Pride is also an obstacle to keeping your promises.

00:29:17.279 --> 00:29:20.799
One of the most typical forms of pride

00:29:21.520 --> 00:29:28.240
in the monastery, where this work was mainly taught,

00:29:28.960 --> 00:29:33.920
is the amount of your knowledge about the scriptures, how many facts you have already gathered

00:29:34.560 --> 00:29:35.780
in your life.

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:39.920
I, for example, love to collect obscure Dharma facts,

00:29:39.920 --> 00:29:41.760
and the more you acquire,

00:29:42.100 --> 00:29:45.760
the more special you feel.

00:29:46.559 --> 00:29:51.487
Pabogka Rinpoche says: "All the Dharma you have ever learned in your life, all the things you have memorized,

00:29:51.487 --> 00:29:53.300
all the things you have debated,

00:29:53.300 --> 00:29:55.360
all the Geshe degrees you can earn:

00:29:57.100 --> 00:30:02.820
compared to what there is still to learn, you know nothing.

00:30:03.100 --> 00:30:06.160
You are like a worm on the ocean floor that

00:30:06.880 --> 00:30:10.700
sometimes swims to the surface and looks at the stars.

00:30:11.520 --> 00:30:14.240
Many of these stars are surrounded by planets.

00:30:15.120 --> 00:30:19.039
There are people on these planets. There are
things to know about these people.

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:23.100
The things we know,

00:30:23.280 --> 00:30:25.860
this knowledge we are so proud of,

00:30:26.240 --> 00:30:32.420
all of this is just a tiny fraction of what you could know.

00:30:33.820 --> 00:30:35.840
So don't be proud.

00:30:35.840 --> 00:30:37.840
The next image.

00:30:41.680 --> 00:30:45.880
One of the great motivations for breaking your promises,

00:30:46.240 --> 00:30:52.880
your vows, your ethics, the thing that will keep you from reaching Nirvana, the thing that will keep you from

00:30:53.760 --> 00:30:56.260
reaching the second stage of Lam Rim: your personal Nirvana,

00:30:57.279 --> 00:31:01.518
is not understanding emptiness! Therefore,  Study emptiness.

00:31:02.960 --> 00:31:04.960
When you realize that the mean things

00:31:05.440 --> 00:31:07.440
someone does to you

00:31:08.080 --> 00:31:11.880
come directly from what you did last week,

00:31:12.480 --> 00:31:16.900
you won't make big mistakes.
The more you study emptiness, the

00:31:17.519 --> 00:31:21.059
more you study cause and effect, dependent origination—

00:31:21.680 --> 00:31:23.920
which means: This person comes from my seed!—the

00:31:24.980 --> 00:31:32.320
easier it will be to keep your promises. The easier it will be, so study, study, study.

00:31:34.160 --> 00:31:39.960
I had a teacher, an old teacher from Mongolia, he was very old and had tuberculosis, and

00:31:45.360 --> 00:31:47.279
he said:

00:31:47.279 --> 00:31:54.879
"He is really good."  You're so proud, you have this huge mountain of pride, from Princeton and

00:31:55.600 --> 00:31:57.279
later from this Geshe thing,

00:31:57.279 --> 00:31:59.279
which is very helpful, very helpful...

00:31:59.340 --> 00:32:02.480
you'll try harder,

00:32:03.039 --> 00:32:05.039
just to look smart.

00:32:05.120 --> 00:32:10.200
That's quite lucky, but later on, stop doing that.  "

00:32:10.500 --> 00:32:13.740
Just learn to be a good person." That was very funny.

00:32:14.760 --> 00:32:17.520
He gave me Adam's text on his deathbed.

00:32:18.320 --> 00:32:20.320
I remember.

00:32:22.559 --> 00:32:24.480
The next picture.

00:32:24.480 --> 00:32:28.959
This is technically the 4th cause, right? No.

00:32:29.040 --> 00:32:35.560
One of the reasons you break or lose your vows is:

00:32:36.160 --> 00:32:38.240
It's very difficult in the modern world to

00:32:38.799 --> 00:32:44.479
keep your mind on your vows when you have a lot to do, when everything has to be done quickly. There

00:32:45.120 --> 00:32:47.439
are a thousand things to look at on the internet,

00:32:48.240 --> 00:32:51.680
and life is moving so fast.

00:32:52.040 --> 00:32:57.220
It's hard to maintain that self-awareness: Am

00:32:57.220 --> 00:33:01.760
I breaking my vows right now, am I doing something that will hurt someone else?

00:33:02.400 --> 00:33:07.260
You need to slow down a little, come back to your vows,

00:33:07.600 --> 00:33:13.300
and maintain a kind of vigilance and sensitivity to

00:33:13.680 --> 00:33:18.420
the fact that you made promises not to hurt others.

00:33:18.740 --> 00:33:22.640
The busier the situation becomes, the more mindful you need to be.

00:33:24.260 --> 00:33:29.697
It's very easy to get annoyed with your partner when you're very busy.

00:33:29.697 --> 00:33:31.840
He or she wants to tell you something,

00:33:32.480 --> 00:33:34.959
and you have to do 10 things at once.  You're working through your tasks and you exclaim,

00:33:36.399 --> 00:33:40.799
"I don't have time to listen to you right now.

00:33:41.360 --> 00:33:44.479
My boss has given me ten things to do."

00:33:45.039 --> 00:33:47.039
These are exactly the times when you need to slow down,

00:33:47.840 --> 00:33:49.840
when you need to remember your vows. Above

00:33:49.919 --> 00:33:53.518
all, don't forget your promise to be kind to others,

00:33:54.240 --> 00:33:57.860
even when you're very stressed and very busy.

00:33:58.480 --> 00:34:03.040
It's better to break business promises

00:34:04.320 --> 00:34:08.720
than to be nervous, stressed, and unkind to others.

00:34:09.839 --> 00:34:12.719
It's better to not pay a bill, or miss a business meeting,

00:34:13.679 --> 00:34:16.158
or not be quite as good at work as you could be

00:34:17.280 --> 00:34:22.160
if that means keeping your mind clear.

00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:25.600
The next picture.

00:34:26.079 --> 00:34:29.379
A woman buying a useless thing at a store.

00:34:31.839 --> 00:34:33.839
Try to remember the story.

00:34:35.359 --> 00:34:40.639
She says, "Oh, this box is so beautiful." She goes to the department store and buys it.

00:34:41.200 --> 00:34:43.200
...what's the name of that store

00:34:43.600 --> 00:34:47.080
where you can buy things like that? Crate and Barrel.

00:34:47.680 --> 00:34:52.560
She goes to Crate and Barrel in the USA. She says, "Oh, my husband will love this box."

00:34:53.120 --> 00:34:56.100
She has no idea what for.  She will use them,

00:34:56.560 --> 00:34:58.560
but she takes them home with her.

00:35:02.960 --> 00:35:08.020
Then she comes home and her husband says, "Are you crazy?"  This is a completely useless box.

00:35:08.020 --> 00:35:14.920
We have enough trash in our house.  Bring them back.  "Get your money back."

00:35:15.440 --> 00:35:22.340
Should she drive to the gas station and try to return the box there?

00:35:22.800 --> 00:35:29.520
No, because that's not where she bought it. This is obvious, but we still have to say it.

00:35:30.080 --> 00:35:32.080
If you buy a stupid box

00:35:32.720 --> 00:35:36.880
because you like it and you think your husband will like it, but he doesn't...

00:35:37.520 --> 00:35:40.460
And if he asks you to return the box, do

00:35:40.720 --> 00:35:44.640
n't take it to another store. Take it back to where you bought it.

00:35:45.280 --> 00:35:51.820
What does that mean?

00:35:54.080 --> 00:35:56.580
You should pay me!

00:35:58.240 --> 00:36:00.240
When it's time for a confession,

00:36:00.240 --> 00:36:02.079
if you've broken a vow,

00:36:02.080 --> 00:36:05.480
try to do it with the person who gave you the vow.

00:36:05.760 --> 00:36:10.620
Confess in the presence of the person who gave you the vow.

00:36:10.860 --> 00:36:15.940
Is it okay to confess to myself at home?

00:36:16.240 --> 00:36:20.920
Not for vows you took from other people!

00:36:21.280 --> 00:36:25.860
Generally speaking, if you didn't take a vow from someone else,

00:36:25.860 --> 00:36:27.660
it might be okay

00:36:27.920 --> 00:36:32.600
to confess at home, in front of a Buddha statue or something like that.  In extreme cases, that's okay.

00:36:33.040 --> 00:36:34.620
But generally speaking,

00:36:35.120 --> 00:36:38.340
if you can go to the person who gave you your vows

00:36:38.640 --> 00:36:43.840
and confess openly to them—then forget the shame. We're shameless all day long.

00:36:44.400 --> 00:36:47.760
Forget the shame about your vows and tell yourself, "What the hell?"

00:36:48.480 --> 00:36:51.280
Go straight to your teacher and say, "I broke this pesky vow."

00:36:51.840 --> 00:36:55.660
And your teacher is like, "Wow, you're a really bad person." And you're like, "Yeah, that's right!"

00:36:56.000 --> 00:37:01.680
Get it over with, and then you'll feel so pure, you'll feel so good.

00:37:02.120 --> 00:37:05.940
You can be shy about many things in life, but don't be shy about your vows.

00:37:05.940 --> 00:37:09.560
If you break a vow, tell someone,

00:37:09.680 --> 00:37:12.880
and that's how you get rid of it. You get rid of the problem.

00:37:13.120 --> 00:37:18.680
If you keep it to yourself and if you spend more time hiding it

00:37:18.720 --> 00:37:21.840
instead of confessing or keeping it, then that's just stupid,

00:37:22.100 --> 00:37:25.200
and it won't make you feel any better. You won't  Feel it purely.

00:37:26.080 --> 00:37:31.820
Just be open with your teachers: I have this problem. I have this bad habit.

00:37:32.160 --> 00:37:36.560
Then the karma is destroyed, the seed is destroyed.

00:37:36.960 --> 00:37:46.420
Your teacher will say, "I've heard that before, you've told me that before." But persist and tell him or her again.

00:37:46.960 --> 00:37:48.960
Next picture.

00:37:50.400 --> 00:37:56.240
This is about... remember?

00:37:59.600 --> 00:38:03.040
It's about honoring

00:38:03.340 --> 00:38:06.580
the small details of the vows again.

00:38:07.020 --> 00:38:12.260
This, by the way, is a vow for monks to
brush their teeth

00:38:12.260 --> 00:38:14.940
with a stick called a so-shing.

00:38:14.940 --> 00:38:17.040
That's a stick you're supposed to use to brush your teeth.

00:38:17.200 --> 00:38:19.919
You just cut it from a tree and use it.

00:38:20.640 --> 00:38:22.640
That's a toothbrush.

00:38:22.960 --> 00:38:30.040
And the vow says monks should have toothbrushes and brush their teeth.

00:38:30.400 --> 00:38:32.560
It might seem like a small thing:

00:38:33.440 --> 00:38:37.460
"Wait, I'm trying to keep my tantric vow here to get into Amitabha's paradise

00:38:38.160 --> 00:38:41.760
and protect all living beings!" And Buddha says, "Yes, but in the meantime,

00:38:41.760 --> 00:38:44.900
could you please..."  Brush your teeth every day.

00:38:44.900 --> 00:38:48.140
And you think to yourself: That's not exactly a grand vow.

00:38:48.560 --> 00:38:52.340
Yes, but it is precisely the little things that make up the Buddha's paradise.

00:38:52.340 --> 00:38:56.260
It is the small things that Bodhisattvas do,

00:38:56.720 --> 00:38:58.720
those who are kind to others.

00:38:59.620 --> 00:39:02.400
Of course, everyone in the world will

00:39:03.600 --> 00:39:08.380
end a nuclear war if they can.  I mean, that's obvious.

00:39:08.640 --> 00:39:11.500
But are you kind enough as a person

00:39:11.840 --> 00:39:15.020
that you wouldn't even want to subject others to your bad breath

00:39:15.360 --> 00:39:16.980
if it might offend them?

00:39:17.080 --> 00:39:19.300
If you are very sensitive

00:39:19.600 --> 00:39:23.200
about the little things that could hurt other people,

00:39:23.440 --> 00:39:25.840
then we can say that you maintain your ethics.

00:39:26.640 --> 00:39:32.240
And then it's the small details that complete the final brushstrokes

00:39:32.880 --> 00:39:39.180
on your Buddha paradise, which you can see in the next picture.

00:39:40.080 --> 00:39:45.920
This person is decorating a Christmas tree...

00:39:46.340 --> 00:39:50.880
I don't know if you've ever decorated a Christmas tree, but those of us who were raised in the Christian tradition were given

00:39:51.680 --> 00:39:53.680
the task of decorating the Christmas tree by our parents.

00:39:54.400 --> 00:39:57.140
And it's something special to

00:39:57.440 --> 00:40:00.360
hang the last ball.

00:40:00.360 --> 00:40:05.440
Everyone looks at the Christmas tree and asks, "Is it finished?"  and then it's: "Yes, he's finished!".

00:40:06.400 --> 00:40:10.079
But then they say: "Wait, we should hang another one right here!"

00:40:10.720 --> 00:40:14.260
This Christmas ornament

00:40:14.560 --> 00:40:20.520
is your teeth brushing.  It's the small final details

00:40:20.880 --> 00:40:27.280
that you add to your Buddhahood.  It is the little things that the Buddhas create.

00:40:27.280 --> 00:40:30.640
It's not the great things.  It's not the big things.  It is attention

00:40:31.599 --> 00:40:33.599
to the small details

00:40:33.680 --> 00:40:39.880
that make other people happy that creates a Buddha.

00:40:40.160 --> 00:40:43.880
The next picture.

00:40:44.160 --> 00:40:53.760
Try to remember this.  Here's a tip for you: Yamantaka!

00:40:55.680 --> 00:41:00.120
This is a famous Lam Rim story.

00:41:00.480 --> 00:41:04.720
Monks and nuns are to go to the Sojong twice a month and confess to each other, openly,

00:41:05.440 --> 00:41:07.900
what mistakes we have made

00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:11.040
.

00:41:11.600 --> 00:41:13.600
The teacher says:

00:41:13.839 --> 00:41:16.959
They hit the GUNTY,

00:41:17.839 --> 00:41:21.199
a special piece of wood, it looks like a square timber,

00:41:21.840 --> 00:41:26.200
and you hit it with another wooden stick and it goes tong, tong, tong...

00:41:26.640 --> 00:41:32.000
and that is then a bell, an old bell, before bells were made of metal.

00:41:32.000 --> 00:41:36.740
The timber was being felled, and when you heard it,

00:41:36.880 --> 00:41:39.980
you had to go to the Sojong.
They still do that today.

00:41:40.240 --> 00:41:43.460
I built a gunty with my teacher.  He wanted one

00:41:43.840 --> 00:41:46.140
and we built it in the right size;

00:41:46.480 --> 00:41:48.180
you have to follow all sorts of rules.

00:41:48.420 --> 00:41:50.420
If you hear that gunty,

00:41:50.880 --> 00:41:52.880
it will be held that way.

00:41:53.200 --> 00:41:55.980
You hold the gunty here and hit it like this.

00:41:56.560 --> 00:42:00.500
And then all monks and nuns are expected to make their profession of faith.

00:42:00.800 --> 00:42:04.880
So this teacher says: "You have beaten the gunty. Let's go."

00:42:05.120 --> 00:42:07.840
And the student says, "No, I'm not going to confess today."

00:42:08.640 --> 00:42:10.640
The teacher asks: "What?"

00:42:11.040 --> 00:42:15.839
For that is one of the main obligations of a monk, to go to the Sojong.

00:42:16.480 --> 00:42:19.199
The teacher says: "What are you talking about?"
And the student says, "I don't have to go today."

00:42:20.000 --> 00:42:22.740
The teacher says, "What do you mean, you don't have to go today?"

00:42:22.800 --> 00:42:26.440
He says, "Have you already forgotten, you gave me the Yamantaka initiation yesterday?

00:42:26.960 --> 00:42:31.600
I am Yamantaka, I am Buddha. I don't need to go to the Sojong anymore."

00:42:32.480 --> 00:42:36.640
The teacher pulls his ear and says, "Yes, of course, you are Yamanika!

00:42:36.920 --> 00:42:42.800
Yamantika will come with me to the Sojong, right now."

00:42:43.200 --> 00:42:47.060
This means: Don't tell me what a great Tantrika you are,

00:42:47.600 --> 00:42:50.220
and that you are above ethics

00:42:50.229 --> 00:42:52.760
and now have a higher vision -

00:42:53.360 --> 00:42:57.060
that is a completely false concept!

00:42:57.440 --> 00:43:00.720
If you have received a secret initiation,

00:43:01.200 --> 00:43:04.180
then you should go to the Sojong every morning.

00:43:04.380 --> 00:43:07.000
You should go even more often than others.

00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:09.320
Because that is exactly what will

00:43:09.520 --> 00:43:13.440
give you the energy for your tantric practice:
being kind to others

00:43:13.440 --> 00:43:15.280
and admitting when you have made a mistake.

00:43:16.080 --> 00:43:20.340
The next picture.

00:43:21.120 --> 00:43:27.760
That's a sad picture.
We always imagine ethics as the root of

00:43:27.760 --> 00:43:31.360
our practice, the basis of our practice.

00:43:31.800 --> 00:43:34.480
Pabongka Rinpoche sees it exactly the opposite way:

00:43:35.680 --> 00:43:37.335
That is the perfect picture.

00:43:37.340 --> 00:43:40.880
He says: Imagine an apple tree that

00:43:41.040 --> 00:43:44.640
someone has cut in half.  In his example, it was a palm tree.

00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:50.980
Someone had cut it in half and removed the crown.

00:43:51.280 --> 00:43:53.760
You will have no leaves,

00:43:53.980 --> 00:43:56.720
not a single leaf will grow.

00:43:56.960 --> 00:43:58.980
That means you won't have any flowers either.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:03.599
And that's why you won't get any fruit from the blossoms.

00:44:04.400 --> 00:44:06.420
You won't get anything at all.

00:44:06.640 --> 00:44:13.080
A person who is not kind to others, day after day, hour after hour,

00:44:13.360 --> 00:44:18.240
eliminates any possibility of

00:44:18.640 --> 00:44:22.140
reaping these beautiful fruits of their practice.

00:44:22.240 --> 00:44:27.420
The next picture.

00:44:30.640 --> 00:44:33.440
This is about something my teacher asked me...

00:44:35.339 --> 00:44:41.039
Sorry, something I asked my teacher, and I don't know if you remember, but I asked him: You reach

00:44:42.720 --> 00:44:49.120
the first of the five paths, the path of accumulation,

00:44:49.340 --> 00:44:54.060
when you experience a personal tragedy,

00:44:54.380 --> 00:44:57.600
but if you are on the Bodhisattva path,

00:44:58.000 --> 00:45:00.136
you reach it when you attain Bodhichitta.

00:45:00.140 --> 00:45:05.160
And I asked him: I don't understand what is supposed to be tragic about Bodhichitta?

00:45:05.680 --> 00:45:07.680
And he said, "No, no.

00:45:07.920 --> 00:45:11.060
The subject is still a tragedy.

00:45:11.520 --> 00:45:17.840
But it is the tragedy of every living being. Every being in the entire universe

00:45:18.800 --> 00:45:21.680
experiences the same tragedy."

00:45:22.060 --> 00:45:28.520
This shared tragedy is the true beginning of the 5 Paths.

00:45:28.660 --> 00:45:30.840
Reflecting on this tragedy

00:45:31.120 --> 00:45:34.200
is the beginning of the 5 paths for a Bodhisattva.

00:45:34.200 --> 00:45:35.780
So, in reality, it's the same thing.

00:45:36.160 --> 00:45:42.140
The puppy is having a hard time, but now all the puppies in the basket are having a hard time.

00:45:42.560 --> 00:45:44.560
We're all in this together.

00:45:44.720 --> 00:45:48.180
And that is the beginning of Bodhichitta.

00:45:48.660 --> 00:45:52.140
Next picture.

00:45:52.143 --> 00:45:56.860
Here, someone is shaking hands with another person in the office.

00:45:57.440 --> 00:46:03.840
I imagine the woman introduced them to each other: This is Jo, who works in the advertising department,

00:46:03.840 --> 00:46:07.360
and this is Sam, who works in the computer department.

00:46:08.000 --> 00:46:10.000
They shake hands with each other.  Do

00:46:10.720 --> 00:46:12.720
you remember what this is about?

00:46:17.680 --> 00:46:23.119
It's a very nice exercise where we close our eyes

00:46:23.920 --> 00:46:26.639
and think about the person who upsets us the most,

00:46:27.440 --> 00:46:31.780
to find out if we can upset ourselves.  The problem with this type of exercise is

00:46:32.320 --> 00:46:35.460
that after about 10 minutes you forget it's an exercise.

00:46:35.760 --> 00:46:38.400
And you're really upset!

00:46:38.640 --> 00:46:40.640
Let me see if I can manage to upset myself.

00:46:41.200 --> 00:46:42.660
How do you plan to do that?

00:46:42.820 --> 00:46:46.800
I'm thinking about this guy who made things really difficult for me this week.  "Yes, do that."

00:46:47.040 --> 00:46:50.940
Then the person doing the exercise starts to tremble.  You ask: "What's happening right now?"

00:46:51.080 --> 00:46:54.720
I got upset!  The experiment worked.

00:46:55.340 --> 00:46:58.960
If the other person is then your lamb, he or she will say:

00:46:59.680 --> 00:47:03.680
"Find out how it feels when you start thinking about this person."

00:47:04.560 --> 00:47:07.199
How does it feel?  What rises up in your heart?

00:47:08.080 --> 00:47:11.560
I don't know about you, but I feel this little disturbance in my heart.

00:47:11.740 --> 00:47:16.500
It starts with me feeling a kind of unease here and there.

00:47:17.200 --> 00:47:21.600
If I think about a person who has bothered me or a problem that has bothered me,

00:47:22.240 --> 00:47:26.100
then I can intentionally

00:47:26.320 --> 00:47:28.320
create tension within myself.

00:47:28.800 --> 00:47:35.460
He says, "Let's do an exercise. Try to build up tension in your heart,

00:47:35.920 --> 00:47:41.360
then look at that tension and get to know it, as if you were shaking someone's hand.

00:47:41.680 --> 00:47:45.180
Get to know what it feels like

00:47:45.680 --> 00:47:48.560
when a mental poison, a negative emotion,

00:47:49.520 --> 00:47:53.540
starts to rise in your heart, and keep practicing this.

00:47:53.840 --> 00:47:56.710
Once you feel better and you've forgotten about the person,

00:47:56.710 --> 00:47:58.380
think about them again.

00:47:58.800 --> 00:48:00.100
See if you can get upset again.

00:48:00.109 --> 00:48:01.999
See if you can start getting upset again.

00:48:02.559 --> 00:48:07.380
Familiarize yourself with how that feels, shake hands: 'Hello.'"  "This is Geshe Michael."

00:48:07.380 --> 00:48:08.959
Hi. Who are you?

00:48:09.599 --> 00:48:12.576
"I'm about to get upset about this person."

00:48:12.576 --> 00:48:15.679
"Nice to see you."  Now I know what you look like.

00:48:16.240 --> 00:48:19.839
Now I'm warned about you.  "I can avoid you in the future."

00:48:20.400 --> 00:48:22.400
Next picture.

00:48:26.880 --> 00:48:31.260
It's called: Journey to the Center of the Sun.

00:48:31.520 --> 00:48:39.080
The theme of this Lam Rim was: Love in the Time of the Virus.

00:48:39.600 --> 00:48:42.960
The virus is a big deal.
It's spread all over the world.

00:48:43.680 --> 00:48:46.960
I've lived a long life and I thought I'd seen it all.

00:48:47.760 --> 00:48:53.500
I've reached my 60s and thought nothing new was going to happen anymore.

00:48:53.780 --> 00:48:56.600
I'm prepared for anything that could happen.

00:48:56.940 --> 00:49:04.560
I've seen it all and nothing can really upset me anymore. Then this virus comes along and threatens everyone in the world.

00:49:05.200 --> 00:49:11.700
Wow, that's a big deal, it affects the entire planet.

00:49:12.160 --> 00:49:15.700
I don't know if it's happened to you, but it's happened to me.

00:49:15.920 --> 00:49:21.100
It's possibly vice 9, envy,

00:49:22.080 --> 00:49:24.240
to be happy when someone else has a problem.

00:49:24.240 --> 00:49:34.040
When I heard that famous, annoying people were getting sick, I thought, "Hehe,

00:49:34.040 --> 00:49:35.760
I didn't want them to die or anything,"

00:49:36.480 --> 00:49:40.920
but I thought, "See, I told you it's bad to be bad."

00:49:41.520 --> 00:49:45.380
And then I  I caught myself thinking exactly that.

00:49:45.760 --> 00:49:47.800
It feels like a big deal.

00:49:48.100 --> 00:49:54.720
It feels like this problem has spread across the entire planet.

00:49:54.720 --> 00:50:00.540
It feels like it's something difficult for me to handle.

00:50:01.120 --> 00:50:03.120
But we have just now,

00:50:03.200 --> 00:50:06.400
after 10 years of Lam Rim studies,

00:50:06.720 --> 00:50:11.380
entered the path for people with high motivation.

00:50:12.400 --> 00:50:16.380
We will open these studies

00:50:16.640 --> 00:50:19.840
with the concept of bodhichitta. What is bodhichitta?

00:50:19.920 --> 00:50:26.220
It does not mean enlightened mind. Forget that bad translation, that incredibly bad translation.

00:50:26.500 --> 00:50:33.120
It is the desire that I may become a Buddha in order to help countless beings.

00:50:34.319 --> 00:50:36.479
There is a direct experience of it in the same

00:50:37.119 --> 00:50:40.180
way that there is a direct experience of emptiness.

00:50:40.180 --> 00:50:45.440
They are parallel experiences that we

00:50:45.680 --> 00:50:51.600
need to achieve in this lifetime, and, again, you should be in meditation while doing so.

00:50:52.560 --> 00:51:00.800
We are describing an extraordinary... how should we call it... breakthrough...

00:51:01.020 --> 00:51:05.560
a threshold experience,

00:51:05.760 --> 00:51:10.300
where you are in a deep state of meditation.

00:51:10.500 --> 00:51:14.100
Because time and space come from seeds,

00:51:14.320 --> 00:51:16.320
if you are with  You can bypass seeds,

00:51:16.720 --> 00:51:19.280
collapse time and space

00:51:20.080 --> 00:51:24.800
in a meditation that lasts no longer than half an hour.

00:51:25.120 --> 00:51:27.120
You could actually

00:51:27.280 --> 00:51:29.940
visit every person in the universe,

00:51:30.300 --> 00:51:33.520
including animals and insects and birds and fish.

00:51:33.800 --> 00:51:38.000
You could communicate with each one individually,

00:51:38.720 --> 00:51:40.720
within half an hour.

00:51:40.800 --> 00:51:43.459
You could make a commitment to each one.

00:51:44.160 --> 00:51:48.820
You meet them and see that each one is suffering,

00:51:49.000 --> 00:51:54.400
each one has a difficult life and worries about the future.

00:51:55.020 --> 00:51:56.960
You could go to each one individually and say,

00:51:57.600 --> 00:52:00.420
"I've got this, stay calm."

00:52:00.820 --> 00:52:03.140
When I was at university,

00:52:03.920 --> 00:52:07.400
I got a scholarship. They said I only had to work a few hours a week for it.

00:52:07.680 --> 00:52:10.300
But it turned out to be 30 hours a week.

00:52:10.640 --> 00:52:14.720
I had to drive a truck.

00:52:14.960 --> 00:52:19.840
Actually, they first put me in a cafeteria and told me to mop the cafeteria floor.

00:52:19.920 --> 00:52:23.440
I quit within 10 hours. I quit on the first day.

00:52:24.480 --> 00:52:29.040
Then they said I could drive a truck. I said, "That's fun. I'll drive a truck."

00:52:29.360 --> 00:52:33.220
I drove the  Trucks for five years. There was

00:52:33.840 --> 00:52:36.160
this man,

00:52:36.480 --> 00:52:41.480
a full-time university employee named Big John.

00:52:41.940 --> 00:52:49.120
His name was Big John. He was Polish, 6'3", a huge guy.

00:52:49.360 --> 00:52:51.020
Everyone was afraid of him when they saw him.

00:52:51.020 --> 00:52:55.140
But he was really wonderful.

00:52:55.520 --> 00:53:03.060
He brought donuts to work, and he was from Trenton, New Jersey.

00:53:03.440 --> 00:53:08.960
He did the kindest things for us, and he covered for us. Once, we were taking apart a truck.

00:53:09.680 --> 00:53:12.399
We drove the truck into a tree and broke it in two.

00:53:13.040 --> 00:53:18.160
He covered for us: "Oh, those bolts weren't tight."

00:53:18.160 --> 00:53:22.000
I don't know what happened.  The truck broke apart.  It's not her fault.  Do

00:53:22.640 --> 00:53:24.640
n't blame these young men.

00:53:25.040 --> 00:53:27.040
All they did was drive him.

00:53:27.440 --> 00:53:31.599
Then he winked at us and said, "I've got you covered. I've got you boys covered."

00:53:32.240 --> 00:53:35.560
I always think of him when I think about Bodhichitta.  So

00:53:36.260 --> 00:53:40.680
you will directly encounter every living being in the universe.

00:53:41.200 --> 00:53:45.200
And you will say: "Big John has you covered. I'll take care of you. Don't worry."

00:53:45.839 --> 00:53:47.919
Do not worry.  I'll take care of you.

00:53:48.960 --> 00:53:51.421
This is Bodhichitta.  You should have this experience.

00:53:51.421 --> 00:53:54.240
You should work for this experience.  You need to meditate.

00:53:54.880 --> 00:53:56.594
You must study Bodhichitta.

00:53:56.594 --> 00:53:58.880
You must study the Lam Rim on Bodhichitta.

00:53:59.920 --> 00:54:02.000
You must go through all these steps;  To

00:54:03.099 --> 00:54:05.099
exchange yourself with others...

00:54:05.680 --> 00:54:09.780
One day you will have this experience and meet every living being.

00:54:10.400 --> 00:54:13.920
You will say to them: "I'll take care of you. Don't worry. I'll take care of you."

00:54:14.000 --> 00:54:18.559
Big Mike will take care of you, or Big Tim, or Big Seiji.

00:54:19.200 --> 00:54:21.200
Do not worry.  Do

00:54:21.599 --> 00:54:24.078
n't stress.  It's my turn!  That's exactly how it

00:54:25.040 --> 00:54:28.719
feels.  It is a personal commitment.

00:54:29.920 --> 00:54:31.920
Why are we talking about this?

00:54:32.400 --> 00:54:36.160
You will do this in countless worlds.  If you do it, on the day you do it,

00:54:36.720 --> 00:54:40.220
you will do it in countless worlds.

00:54:40.640 --> 00:54:46.960
An action that is a direct obligation to all living creatures in countless worlds

00:54:48.000 --> 00:54:52.820
has no problem dealing with a single virus on a single world.

00:54:52.940 --> 00:54:54.060
That's nothing.

00:54:54.320 --> 00:54:57.200
A virus that threatens 7 or 8 billion people

00:54:57.200 --> 00:55:03.200
is nothing compared to Bodhichitta.

00:55:03.480 --> 00:55:07.180
We said: If you pour ketchup on your shirt

00:55:07.180 --> 00:55:13.920
and put that shirt in the middle of the sun, where it's 15 million degrees Celsius hot,

00:55:14.320 --> 00:55:17.280
then the ketchup stain will probably disappear.

00:55:18.000 --> 00:55:23.600
Then you probably won't have to worry about the ketchup stain anymore.  Work on your Bodhichitta.

00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:27.520
And you will destroy the virus, quite incidentally, quite by chance.

00:55:28.319 --> 00:55:30.319
No big deal.

00:55:30.799 --> 00:55:32.799
Next picture.

00:55:34.160 --> 00:55:36.799
Don't experiment with other methods.

00:55:37.440 --> 00:55:40.620
Learn Bodhichitta.  Learn to have this experience.  Do

00:55:40.880 --> 00:55:42.880
n't waste your time.  Do

00:55:43.520 --> 00:55:47.040
n't focus on other things.  Focus on Bodhichitta.

00:55:47.360 --> 00:55:49.840
Then you don't have to do things twice.

00:55:50.160 --> 00:55:53.840
We talked about doing things twice.  This woman is in a hurry.

00:55:54.240 --> 00:55:57.040
She says: I don't have time for this Bodhichitta stuff.

00:55:57.680 --> 00:56:00.399
I'm going straight into Tantra.

00:56:01.200 --> 00:56:04.790
You will still have to come back to make up for what you forgot,

00:56:04.790 --> 00:56:05.760
and that is Bodhichitta.

00:56:05.760 --> 00:56:08.600
Work on your Bodhichitta first.

00:56:09.040 --> 00:56:16.280
Then you don't have to go back home, pick up the Bodhichitta, and come back.

00:56:18.960 --> 00:56:26.680
Then there's a radical example in the next picture.

00:56:27.520 --> 00:56:31.600
It's difficult to remember this image.  I'll give you a moment to think about it.

00:56:42.400 --> 00:56:46.260
I don't know if you remember that.

00:56:46.560 --> 00:56:48.280
It's complicated.

00:56:48.281 --> 00:56:57.640
A group of 60 men and women were on the verge of reaching Nirvana by directly seeing emptiness

00:56:57.960 --> 00:57:01.960
but without Bodhichitta, i.e., lower Nirvana.

00:57:02.240 --> 00:57:08.000
Manjushri appears and teaches them Bodhichitta.

00:57:08.120 --> 00:57:13.020
Perhaps he learned this from the experience we were just talking about.

00:57:13.280 --> 00:57:17.440
They were all annoyed by Manjushri.  They said, "Don't waste our time.

